[{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>A battery-powered toy car is placed on a straight track. The car is switched on, so that when it contacts the track, it instantly moves with constant velocity. The following graph shows the displacement <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (metres), over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (seconds) of the toy car:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>How far along the track is the car initially placed?</p></li><li><p>How far along the track is the car when 8 seconds have passed?</p></li><li><p>Find the velocity of the car.</p></li><li><p>How far along the track is the car after 5 seconds?</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>2 metres from the start of the track</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>4 metres from the start of the track</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{4-2}{8-0}=0.25\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.25\\times5+2=3.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres</p>","<p>(1.25 metres from where the car started)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Displacement <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (metres) over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (seconds) for a particle is given in the graph below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the distance travelled over the first 20 seconds.</p></li><li><p>the displacement over the first 20 seconds.</p></li><li><p>the average speed of the particle.</p></li><li><p>the velocity for the first part of the motion.</p></li><li><p>the velocity for the second part of the motion.</p></li><li><p>the average velocity of the particle.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16+17+7=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{40}{20}=2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{16}4=4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{24}{16}=-\\frac32\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac8{20}=-\\frac25\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Displacement <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"s\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (metres) over time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (seconds) for a particle is given in the graph below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q3.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find, after the first 10 seconds,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the distance travelled by the particle.</p></li><li><p>the displacement of the particle.</p></li><li><p>the average speed of the particle.</p></li><li><p>the average velocity of the particle.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6+12=18\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>6 m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{18}{10}=1.8\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac6{10}=0.6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Lisa runs in a straight line for 60 seconds at a constant speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. She then pauses for 20 seconds before turning and running in the opposite direction for 45 seconds at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Draw a displacement-time graph to show the athlete's motion.</p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s4.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>A child is running along a straight, flat path. He runs for 6 seconds at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. He then stops and waits for 5 seconds, before running back along the path for 9 seconds, returning to his original starting point.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the displacement-time graph for the motion of the child.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact velocity for the final stage of the motion.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s5a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{12-0}{11-20}=-\\frac43\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>An object travels 20 metres at constant velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> taking <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds. It then pauses and remains stationary for 5 seconds before returning to its original position in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a displacement-time graph for the motion of the object.</p></li><li><p>Given the total time the object is in motion is 6 seconds, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s6a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Stationary for 5 seconds, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac32t+5=11\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\therefore t=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Describe what is happening to the objects in each of the following velocity-time graphs for velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, in metres per second and time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, in seconds. For each stage of motion comment on the speed and where possible its position:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q7a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q7b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The object starts at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and it accelerates uniformly until it reaches <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>It remains at a constant speed until a total of 6 seconds have passed since the start.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The object starts from rest, accelerating at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the first 3 seconds and reaches <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<p>The object travels at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 4 seconds.</p>","<p>The object decelerates at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> uniformly, before reaching a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in 1.5 seconds. It then accelerates in the negative direction at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for a further 1.5 seconds.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>For each of the following velocity-time graphs below, sketch the corresponding acceleration-time graph:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q8a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q8b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s8a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s8b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>For each of the following acceleration-time graphs below, sketch the corresponding velocity-time graph given that the object is initially at rest:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q9a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li><li><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q9b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s9a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s9b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A car which is initially at rest, accelerates at a constant rate of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 3 seconds and then remains at this constant speed.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph to show the first 10 seconds of the motion of the car.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance travelled by the car in the first 10 seconds of motion.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s10a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times3\\times13.5+7\\times13.5=114.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>A cyclist is timed along a section of track, with velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span> recorded in metres per second at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=14\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p><p>The velocity-time graph for the cyclist is shown below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q11.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find the</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>acceleration of the cyclist at each stage.</p></li><li><p>total distance travelled by the cyclist.</p></li><li><p>time when the cyclist is travelling at exactly <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>speed the cyclist is travelling at 17 seconds.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-0.2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac23\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times5\\times10+\\frac12(5+4.2)\\times4+\\frac12(4.2+8.2)\\times6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=80.6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>On the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=0.5t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>On the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v-4.2=\\frac23(t-14)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So if <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=17\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=6.2\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Sketch a velocity-time graph which represents a car initially at rest, with:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>constant acceleration for the first 6 seconds before reaching a fixed velocity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which it remains at for a further <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p></li><li><p>increasing acceleration for the first 2 seconds, constant acceleration for the next 3 seconds, then decreasing acceleration for the next 1 second, before reaching a fixed velocity of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> which it remains at for a further <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s12a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s12b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>The velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at a given time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds of a van in motion on a straight flat road is modelled using the velocity-time graph below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q13.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the deceleration of the van in the first 10 seconds.</p></li><li><p>At 10 seconds, the van continues to travel at a constant speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"18\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for a distance of 1026 m. Find the time it spends at this speed.</p></li><li><p>Find the total distance travelled by the van at the time given in your part b).</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac6{10}=-0.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So deceleration is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.6\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1026}{18}=57\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(24+18)\\times10=210\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1026+210=1236\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>An object is moving in a straight line. It starts at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, before accelerating uniformly to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in 8 seconds, moving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"10\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 5 seconds before finally decelerating to rest in 7 seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph which represents the motion of the object.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance travelled by the object.</p></li><li><p>Find the average velocity of the object.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s14a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(4+10)\\times8+5\\times10+\\frac12\\times7\\times10=141\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{141}{20}=7.05\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>A van is driving along a straight stretch of motorway. It starts at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"33\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, before decelerating to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> uniformly over 1.1 km.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph which represents the motion of the van.</p></li><li><p>Find the time the van spends decelerating according to this model.</p></li></ol><p>The van then maintains this speed for a further 400 metres.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><p>Find the average speed of the van.</p></li><li><p>Two speed cameras, one at the start and one at the end of this 1.5 km stretch of road, measure the speed of the van and finds its average. Find this speed.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s15a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1100=\\frac12(33+22)\\times t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"22\\times T=400\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=\\frac{200}{11}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So total time is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"40+\\frac{200}{11}=\\frac{640}{11}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Average speed is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1500\\div\\frac{640}{11}=\\frac{825}{32}=25.8\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times(33+22)=27.5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>A vehicle is being driven along a flat, straight road. Its motion is modelled using the velocity-time graph below where velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given in metres per second and time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given in seconds.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q16.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration at each stage of motion.</p></li><li><p>Find the total distance driven by the vehicle in the first 20 seconds.</p></li><li><p>Find the total distance driven by the vehicle in the final 15 seconds.</p></li><li><p>State the displacement of the vehicle at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p></li><li><p>State the displacement of the vehicle at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=35\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p></li><li><p>State the total distance driven by the vehicle.</p></li><li><p>Find the average speed of the vehicle over the 35 seconds.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac65=1.2\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{11}{22}=-0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac55=1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15+18+36=69\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"25+12.5=37.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>69 m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"69-37.5=31.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"69+37.5=106.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{106.5}{35}=3.04\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> (3 SF)</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>A cyclist starts from rest and is cycling along a flat straight road. He accelerates at a constant acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the first 5 seconds, before accelerating at a constant acceleration of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.3\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the next 5 seconds. He then remains at a constant speed for a further 20 m.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph to model the motion of the bicycle.</p></li><li><p>State the velocity of the cyclist in the third stage of the motion.</p></li><li><p>Find how far the cyclist has cycled since the initial start point.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s17a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times5\\times2.5+\\frac12(2.5+4)\\times5+20=42.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>The velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at a given time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds of a car in motion is modelled using the velocity-time graph below.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q18.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the acceleration for all three stages of the motion.</p></li><li><p>the exact times at which the car, according to the graph has instantaneously stopped.</p></li><li><p>the total distance travelled by the car.</p></li><li><p>the displacement of the car from its initial position.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{21}7=-3\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac6{12}=0.5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=-3t+30\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=24\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(10+5)\\times15+\\frac12\\times14\\times6=112.5+42\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"=154.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"112.5-42=70.5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>A ride at a theme park with a 35 second duration has a carriage that travels along a flat, straight track.</p><p>The velocity-time graph below shows the motion of the carriage in time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in seconds.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q19.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the maximum magnitude of acceleration over the 35 second ride.</p></li><li><p>Find the times at which the carriage is instantaneously stationary.</p></li><li><p>If the passengers disembark at 35 seconds, where are they in relation to the start point?</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac{25}5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so max acceleration is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>On line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=-5t+62\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=12.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=12.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=35\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(4+12.4)\\times12-\\frac12(3+22.6)\\times13=-68\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<p>So 68 m before the initial start point.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>A bus travels from rest from a bus stop, on a straight, flat road. It drives with acceleration <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0.9\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for 15 seconds. It is then driven at constant velocity before decelerating uniformly at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where it comes to rest at a second bus stop which is 918 metres from the first bus stop.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the velocity of the bus when it is moving with constant velocity.</p></li><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph to represent the motion of the bus.</p></li><li><p>Find the time taken to get between the bus stops.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\times0.9=13.5\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s20b.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(T+13.5+(T-15))\\times13.5=918\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T+13.5+T-15=136\\Rightarrow2T=\\frac{275}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow T=68.75\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So total time is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"68.75+13.5=82.25\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>The velocity-time graph shows the motion of a runner running along a straight flat track of length 200 metres before coming to a stop.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q21.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>The runner accelerates uniformly from rest over the first 15 metres until reaching a speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> before continuing to run at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> until they complete the 200 m. A further 3 seconds later they come to rest. Find</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the exact time the runner completes the 200 metres.</p></li><li><p>the total distance they run.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times t_1\\times6=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t_1=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> s</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(t_2-5)\\times6=200-15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t_2=\\frac{215}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=35\\frac16\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\times3\\times6=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so 209 metres</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>An object starts from rest and is travelling in a straight line with uniform acceleration for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds, travelling 24 metres. It then moves with constant velocity for 9 seconds before coming to rest uniformly in a further <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac35T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch a velocity-time graph for the motion of the object.</p></li><li><p>Given the displacement of the object is 146.4 metres, find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s22a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\left(\\frac85T+9+9\\right)\\times\\frac{48}T=146.4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Rightarrow\\frac85T+9+9=6.1T\\Rightarrow18=4.5T\\Rightarrow T=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>Two cars, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are driving along a straight, flat road.</p><p>Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is driving with constant velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which is initially driving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"12\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, is driving with constant acceleration until 32 seconds have passed at which it then drives at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"20\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><p>The velocity-time graph demonstrating the motion of the two cars is shown below:</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/questions/assets/diagrams/q23.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the acceleration of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the first 32 seconds of the motion.</p></li><li><p>Find the equation that gives the velocity of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for the first 32 seconds of motion.</p></li><li><p>Find the exact time at which car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> overtakes car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> according to the model.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance the cars have travelled when car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> overtakes car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>State what the point of intersection of the two lines represents.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac8{32}=0.25\\text{ ms}^{-2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=0.25t+12\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Overtake at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when they have travelled the same distance:</p>","<p>As areas must be equal, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t&lt;32\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(12+12+0.25t)\\times t=12t+0.125t^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15t=12t+0.125t^2\\Rightarrow t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=24\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>so at 24 s</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\times24=360\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>The time at which both cars are instantaneously driving at the same speed of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year1-1.64-q24","number":24,"question":"<p>Two cars, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are driving along a straight, flat road. Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is driving with constant velocity <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which is initially driving at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(u-5)\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, is driving with constant acceleration until <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds have passed at which it then drives at a constant velocity. Car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> overtakes car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at exactly <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> seconds.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Sketch the velocity-time graph for the two cars.</p></li><li><p>State the velocity of car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when it overtakes car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Given that the cars are going the same speed exactly when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=20\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and car B overtakes car <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> after driving 1000 m, find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-1.64/solutions/assets/diagrams/s24a.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Overtake at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when they have travelled the same distance, so by symmetry <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"v=(u+5)\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T=2\\times20=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"u\\times40=1000\\Rightarrow u=25\\text{ ms}^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]}]